<article class="env-definition" id="04JV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04JV">Definition <span data-tag="04JV">66.19.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\overline{x}$ be a geometric point of $X$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An <em>étale neighborhood</em> of $\overline{x}$ of $X$ is a commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ &  U \ar[d]^\varphi \\  {\bar x} \ar[r]^{\bar x} \ar[ur]^{\bar u} &  X }  \]
</div>
<p>
 where $\varphi $ is an étale morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. We will use the notation $\varphi : (U, \overline{u}) \to (X, \overline{x})$ to indicate this situation. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism of étale neighborhoods</em> $(U, \overline{u}) \to (U', \overline{u}')$ is an $X$-morphism $h : U \to U'$ such that $\overline{u}' = h \circ \overline{u}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>